and performance in dark shots with the car and kerb impact.\n\n\nAdjusted exposure curves for several shots to address clipping and improve luminance, specifically focusing on specific frames. Enhanced shot S21 by increasing EV, significantly increasing mean luminance and P95. Reduced clipping percentage in shot S22 with a negative EV adjustment.\n\nUpdated halftone rendering parameters to ensure that Ben-Day halftone dots are unmistakably visible across midtone transitions in the 1080p resolution. Adjusted parameters to enhance color separation and the visual effects of portals in the composite script.\n\n\nAct I introduces a warm crimson/amber wash at 0.48 intensity, transitioning to a warmer RGB profile. Act II implements a bright aquamarine/mint-teal and hot-pink/peach wash with a blend effect for an airy watercolor feel at 0.64 intensity. Act III features a laser-crimson/vermilion wash at 0.58 intensity with obsidian-ultraviolet accents.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"read_file","args":{"EndLine":1715,"Path":"d:\\项目session\\blender-supercar\\pipeline\\v6_sv_comp.py","StartLine":1420}}]}
